s fast and generates audio + video together. But **Wan 2.2** currently produces the best quality among all open-source options.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Where to Run Them FOR FREE (No GPU on Your PC? No Problem)\\n\\n| Platform | Free GPU | VRAM | Weekly Limit | Best For |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Google Colab** | NVIDIA T4 | 16GB | ~12h sessions, unlimited | Quick prototyping |\\n| **Kaggle Notebooks** | P100 / 2×T4 | 16GB | ~30 hours/week | More reliable, predictable |\\n| **Hugging Face Spaces** | H200 (ZeroGPU) | Varies | Limited quota | Running demos |\\n\\n### How to Use (Simplest Path):\\n1. Go to [Google\n<truncated 2913 bytes>","Description":"\"Research report on open-source video generation models as free alternatives to Google Flow\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\9b49962f-2973-4675-be85-0cd52ae6804d\\\\open_source_video_research.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating artifact\"","toolSummary":"\"Research report artifact\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
