{"step_index":57,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:36:30Z","content":"Here's the short answer:\n\n### Yes — open-source models are your best path to free, unlimited video generation.\n\n**Your LTX-2.5 is a good pick**, but **Wan 2.2** (Alibaba) is currently the best open-source model — it produces ~85% of Veo/Flow quality, completely free.\n\n### The problem: You need a GPU\nThese models need an NVIDIA GPU with 16GB+ VRAM to run. **If you don't have one**, use these free cloud options:\n- **Google Colab** — free T4 GPU (16GB), no billing needed\n- **Kaggle Notebooks** — free P100 GPU, 30 hours/week\n\nJust search \"Wan 2.1 Colab notebook\" on Hugging Face, open it, type your prompt, and download the `.mp4`.\n\n### How Remotion + FFmpeg help you\n\n```\nAI Model (raw 5-10s clips) → FFmpeg (stitch + compress) → Remotion (text, transitions, branding)\n```\n\n- **AI model** = generates the raw video clips\n- **FFmpeg** = stitches clips together, adds music, compresses for YouTube\n- **Remotion** = adds animated text, captions, motion graphics, transitions\n\nThis is a **complete zero-cost video pipeline** — no Google billing, no Flow credits, no API charges. I've saved a detailed research report in your artifacts with model comparisons, GPU requirements, and pricing."}
